Description: This Terraform configuration creates an S3 source bucket represented as `a`, creates a separate S3 bucket named `logging-680235478471` to receive access logs, grants the S3 logging service permission to write logs into the logging bucket, and configures server access logging on the source bucket using the `log/` prefix.

Note: AWS S3 bucket names must be globally unique and at least 3 characters long, so the deployable bucket name defaults to `a-680235478471`. The Terraform resource itself is named `a`.

